      <contributor>
        <ip>86.132.229.20</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Shabeellaha Hoose''', or '''Lower Shabele''', is a region (''gobolka'') in southern [[Somalia]]. Until [[1984]]when the regions were reshaped by the then military regime it was part of the larger Benadir region and its capital was [[Mogadishu]], but is now [[Marka]]. It is bordered by the Somalian regions of [[Banaadir 'Mogadishu']], [[Shabeellaha Dhexe]], [[Hiiraan]], [[Bay, Somalia|Bay]] and [[Jubbada Dhexe]] and the [[Indian Ocean]]. After Mogadishu, this is thought to be the region with the most population in Somalia. The Digil sub-clan of the Rahanwein clan make up most of the population.

==Its distrcits are==

*[[Barawe]]
*[[Marka (Capital)]]
*Qoriyoley
*Janale
*Sablale
*Kurtunwarey


{{Somalia Regions}}	 

{{AfricaE-geo-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
