      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Adana Turkey Provinces locator.jpg|thumb|300px|shows the Location of the Province Adana]]
'''Adana Province''' is a [[Provinces of Turkey|province]] located in south-eastern [[Turkey]]. The provinces adjacent to it are [[Mersin Province|Mersin]] to the west, [[Hatay Province|Hatay]] to the southeast, [[Osmaniye Province|Osmaniye]] to the east, [[Kahramanmaraş Province|Kahramanmaraş]] to the northeast, and [[Kayseri Province|Kayseri]] to the north. Its capital is the city of  '''[[Adana]]'''. [[NATO]]'s [[Incirlik Air Base]] is located within this province.

Other important cities in this province include Ayas/[[Issus]], and [[Kozan, Adana|Kozan]] (formerly Sis).

The name of Adana is thought to come from Adanus, the son of Uranus (the Greek god of heaven).

Adana is famous for its kebab and salgam. [[Turnip juice|Salgam]] is a salty purple juice made from purple carrots.

[[Osmaniye Province]] was formerly part of Adana Province.

