      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''Eurovision Song Contest 1986''' was the 31st [[Eurovision Song Contest]] and was held on [[May 3]], [[1986]] in [[Bergen, Norway|Bergen]], [[Norway]]. The presenter was [[Åse Kleveland]].  [[Sandra Kim]] was the winner of this Eurovision with the song, [[J'aime La Vie]]. Aged 13, Sandra was the youngest ever Eurovision winner. Current rules require Eurovision Song Contest participants to be at least 15, so unless the rule is changed Kim's record will never be broken. In the lyrics of her song, Kim claimed to be 15 years of age, but when it was revealed that she was actually 13 after the contest, [[Switzerland]] appealed for her to be disqualified, but this was to no avail.

