  <page>
    <title>Moon Mullins</title>
    <id>185284</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33810767</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-04T05:39:56Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Xaosflux</username>
        <id>502540</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted edits by [[Special:Contributions/67.98.183.77|67.98.183.77]] to last version by Doughboy</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''Moon Mullins''''', by [[Frank Willard]], ran as a daily and Sunday [[comic strip]] from [[1923]] to [[1991]]. Irish immigrant Moon, with his pug face and derby hat, got into endless scrapes, none of them fatal or even particularly threatening. Indeed, the gentleness of the humor behind the rough scenes kept the strip on an even keel. Moon's little brother, Kayo, slept in the bottom drawer of Moon's bureau and was, at heart, a good deal more of the ruffian than was Moon.



[[Category:Comic strips]]
[[Category:Comics characters|Mullins, Moon]]

&lt;div class=&quot;boilerplate&quot; id=&quot;stub&quot;&gt; ''This [[comic strip]]-related article is a [[Wikipedia:stub|stub]]. You can [[Wikipedia:Find or fix a stub|help]] Wikipedia by [{{SERVER}}{{localurl:{{NAMESPACE}}:{{PAGENAME}}|action=edit}} expanding it]''. &lt;/div&gt;</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>His</title>
