      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;
&lt;caption&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;+1&quot;&gt;'''Vivienne Poy'''&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/caption&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;background:#efefef;&quot; align=&quot;center&quot; colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Senatorial Division:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[Toronto]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Appointed by:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[Jean Chrétien]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Public Telephone:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;943-7854&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Public E-Mail:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;poyv@sen.parl.gc.ca&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Date of nomination:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[September 17]], [[1998]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Expected date of retirement:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[May 15]], [[2016]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Date of Birth:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[1941]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Place of Birth:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;[[Hong Kong]]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Spouse:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Neville Poy&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;'''Previous [[Profession]]:'''&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Fashion Designer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

[[The Honourable]] '''Vivienne Poy''', [[Master of Arts|MA]] n&amp;eacute;e Lee (利德蕙; [[Cantonese language|Cantonese]] [[Yale Romanization#Cantonese Yale|Yale]]:  Ley6 Dak1-way6;  [[Mandarin language|Mandarin]] [[Pinyin]]: Lì Déhuì), (born [[1941]] in [[Hong Kong]]) was appointed to the [[Canadian Senate|Senate of Canada]] in [[1998]]. Poy came to Canada as a university student in [[1959]]. She is the first Canadian senator of [[Asian Canadian|Asian ancestry]]. She graduated from [[St. Paul's Co-educational College]], [[McGill University]], [[Seneca College]] and [[University of Toronto]].

For 14 years, Poy served as president of [[Vivienne Poy Mode]], a [[fashion]] design company that she founded in [[1981]].  She was selected as [[Chancellor]] of the [[University of Toronto]] in December [[2002]].

Poy is the daughter of [[Richard Charles Lee]] (利銘澤; [[pinyin]]: L&amp;#464; Míngzé), who is the son of famous businessman [[Hysan Lee]] in [[Hong Kong]], and [[Esther Yewpick Lee]] (黃瑤璧) and the sister-in-law of [[Adrienne Clarkson]], who was [[Governor General of Canada]] from [[1999]] to [[2005]]. Vivienne Poy's husband Dr. [[Neville Poy]], a retired plastic surgeon, is [[Adrienne Clarkson]]'s brother.

See also [[List of Ontario senators]].

== See also ==
