      <text xml:space="preserve">The 45th [[Grammy]] Awards were held on [[February 23]], [[2003]]. They recognized accomplishments by musicians from the previous year. 

==Award winners:==

*[[Grammy Award for Record of the Year|Record of the Year]]
**[[Arif Mardin]] (producer), [[Jay Newland]] (producer &amp; engineer/mixer), [[Norah Jones]] (producer &amp; artist) for &quot;Don't Know Why&quot;

* [[Grammy Award for Album of the Year|Album of the Year]]
**[[Arif Mardin]], [[Craig Street]] (producers), [[Jay Newland]] (engineer/mixer &amp; producer), [[S. Husky Höskulds]] (engineer/mixer), [[Ted Jensen]] (mastering engineer) &amp; [[Norah Jones]] (producer &amp; artist) for ''Come Away With Me''

* [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]]
**[[Jesse Harris]] (songwriter) for &quot;Don't Know Why&quot; performed by [[Norah Jones]]

* [[Grammy Award for Best New Artist|Best New Artist]]
**[[Norah Jones]]

===Special Merit Awards===

*[[Grammy Lifetime Achievement Award|Lifetime Achievement Award]]
**[[Etta James]]
**[[Johnny Mathis]]
**[[Glenn Miller]]
**[[Tito Puente]]
**[[Simon &amp; Garfunkel]]

*[[Grammy Trustees Award|Trustees Award]]
**[[Alan Lomax]] 
**The [[New York Philharmonic]]

*[[Grammy Legend Award|Legend Award]]
**[[Bee Gees]]

*[[Grammy Tech Award|Tech Award]]
**[[Geoff Emerick]]
**[[Shure Incorporated]]

===Alternative===

*[[Grammy Award for Best Alternative Music Album|Best Alternative Music Album]] 
**[[Ken Nelson]] (producer &amp; engineer/mixer), [[Mark Phythian]] (engineer/mixer) &amp; [[Coldplay]] (producers, engineers/mixers &amp; artists) for ''[[A Rush of Blood to the Head]]''

===Blues===

