      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''Hong Kong Sevens''' (香港七人欖球賽) is generally considered the premier tournament on the [[World Sevens Series]] in [[Rugby Union]]. It is held annually in [[Hong Kong]], around [[Easter]].

In 1997 and 2005, the Hong Kong Sevens was not held; taking its place was the [[International Rugby Board|IRB]] [[Rugby World Cup Sevens]], which Hong Kong hosted in both years. Fiji won both World Cup Sevens tournaments held in Hong Kong.

Established in [[1976]], it originally was contested by teams in the Asian-Pacific region. Since the late 1980s the tournament has featured 24 teams from all over the world. 

One of the enduring traditions in the tournament is the ritualistic booing of the [[Australia|Australian]] team. During the event, the South Stands of [[Hong Kong Stadium]] are famous for the chanting crowds in colourful costumes. Generally they are lashed off their faces due to the pitchers of pimms and fosters on sale at cheap prices.

==Past Champions==
*1976 Cantabrians (provincial team from New Zealand)
*1977 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1978 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1979 [[Australian national rugby union team (sevens)|Australia]]
*1980 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1981 Barbarians (mixed side from the United Kingdom)
*1982 [[Australian national rugby union team (sevens)|Australia]]
*1983 [[Australian national rugby union team (sevens)|Australia]]
*1984 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1985 [[Australian national rugby union team (sevens)|Australia]]
*1986 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1987 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1988 [[Australian national rugby union team (sevens)|Australia]]
*1989 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1990 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1991 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1992 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1993 Samoa
*1994 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1995 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1996 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*1997 ''Not held'' &amp;ndash; see [[Rugby World Cup Sevens]]
*1998 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*1999 [[Fiji national rugby union team (sevens)|Fiji]]
*2000 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*2001 [[New Zealand national rugby union team (sevens)|New Zealand]]
*2002 [[England national rugby union team (sevens)|England]]
*2003 [[England national rugby union team (sevens)|England]]
*2004 [[England national rugby union team (sevens)|England]]
*2005 ''Not held'' &amp;ndash; see [[Rugby World Cup Sevens]]

==See also==
* [[Rugby Sevens]]
* [[World Sevens Series]]
* [[Rugby World Cup Sevens]]
==External Links==
